home to many of the gods in Greek  mythology Mount Olympus was created  after the war between the Olympians and  the Titans a war that finally ended  after ten years and saw Zeus and his  fellow Olympians victorious Olympus is  often described as containing a fabulous  palaces made of marble and gold  mythicist  the highest of all of its peaks was  referred to as the pantheon this is  where the gods would gather and many  fierce discussions and arguments took  place within the pantheon there are many  gods and goddesses who were believed to  have lived on Mount Olympus it is the  twelve Olympians were most commonly  depicted as making Mount Olympus their  home with Poseidon and Hades chosen to  live separately  [Music]  the ancient Greek poem Iliad describes  Olympus has been an ancient Acropolis  essentially a fortified hilltop somewhat  of a palace complex located just below  the peaks of Mount Olympus located on  the lowest level of the mountain or the  nine Muses  who would often entertain the gods of  Olympus the golden gates that led to  Olympus were not guarded by any creature  or monster  they were guarded by the three goddesses  of the seasons the main feature to  Olympus was indeed Lucis palace much  larger than the palaces of the other  gods and goddesses despite the size  Lucis palace still had a very simple  layout with a large central hall private  bed chambers and some storage rooms the  main hall had floors made from gold and  often served as a council chamber and a  feast hall for the other Olympian gods  as it provided them with an expansive  view of the world allowing them to  observe mankind from the heights of  Olympus the tables and furniture of the  Great Hall were created by the divine  smyth Hephaestus and they were animated  so they could present themselves when  needed and packed themselves away when  the feasts were over  outside the palaces of Olympus was a  lush land teeming of exotic fruits and  herds of cattle there was a large  courtyard where all the gods would  gather including those of Earth and even  the sea deities sometimes even nymphs  were invited Olympus was more than a  lush land filled with exotic fruit and  vegetation the gods had an abundance of  anything that they would have ever  needed to the gods Olympus was just the  home that they deserved nothing more and  nothing less to everyone else Olympus  was a paradise that they only wish they  could have visited Mount Olympus is  indeed an actual Mountain located in  Greece the highest in the country there  are those who believe that the gods  never lived on the mountain  Olympus knows more as a metaphor as it  reflects the social hierarchy in Greek  mythology Mount Olympus been the highest  point would naturally make sense as home  of the gods as they are elevated above  all mortals creatures and demigods able  to look down at those they were  considered to be above and rule over  [Music]
 

